  "asOf": "2026-10-01",
  "about": "Answers docs/research/requests/migration-rates-and-reasons.json parts (1) and (2) for the two rates the quarterly migration review reads (src/simulation/migration/review.ts): how many of a place's residents leave for another county or state in a year, by age band, and how many newcomers arrive from another county, state or abroad per resident. Each of the 50 states, D.C. and Puerto Rico has its own rates from the American Community Survey 2024 one-year estimates; Guam, the U.S. Virgin Islands, American Samoa and the Northern Mariana Islands, which the survey does not cover, take the national rates, marked ESTIMATED FROM AVERAGE. Rates are a check on totals across a town's residents and set how strongly each resident's age weighs on leaving; they are not one person's fate.",
  "sources": {
    "departure": {
      "table": "B07401 Geographical Mobility in the Past Year by Age for Residence 1 Year Ago in the United States (Puerto Rico: B07401PR)",
      "url": "https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/2024/table-based-SF/data/1YRData/acsdt1y2024-b07401.dat",
      "urlPuertoRico": "https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/2024/table-based-SF/data/1YRData/acsdt1y2024-b07401pr.dat",
      "method": "For each age band from 18 and 19 through 75 and over, the residents who moved to a different county in the same state plus those who moved to a different state (Puerto Rico: to a different municipio plus to the United States), over everyone in that band who lived in the place a year earlier. Moves within the same county and moves abroad are not counted: the first may not leave town, and the survey cannot reach the second.",
      "quote": "B07401_049|Moved to different county within same state: ... B07401_065|Moved to different state:",
      "shellsUrl": "https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/2024/table-based-SF/documentation/ACS20241YR_Table_Shells.txt"
    },
    "arrivals": {
